Creates a standalone HTML page that displays CFB spreads data from `cfb model output_new.csv` with interactive features for analysis.

## Changes

- **`index.html`** - Self-contained page (no external dependencies) with:
  - Sortable table: click headers to sort ascending/descending (↕ ↑ ↓)
  - Real-time search filtering across all columns
  - Color-coded gradients for "Cover Probability (%)" and "Edge (%)" columns:
    - Red (negative values) → Green (positive values)
    - Intensity scales with magnitude
  - Auto-refresh every 5 minutes + manual refresh button
  - Mobile-responsive with horizontal scrolling
  - Fetches from: `https://raw.githubusercontent.com/trashduty/trash-schedule/main/cfb%20model%20output_new.csv`

- **`README.md`** - GitHub Pages setup instructions

## Color Gradient Implementation

```javascript
function getColorForValue(value) {
    const numValue = parseFloat(value);
    if (isNaN(numValue)) return { backgroundColor: 'transparent', color: 'inherit' };

    let r, g, b;
    if (numValue < 0) {
        // Negative: darker red as magnitude increases
        const intensity = Math.min(Math.abs(numValue) * 10, 1);
        r = Math.round(255 * Math.min(intensity * 2, 1));
        g = Math.round(50 * (1 - Math.min(intensity, 1)));
        b = Math.round(50 * (1 - Math.min(intensity, 1)));
    } else {
        // Positive: darker green as magnitude increases
        const intensity = Math.min(numValue * 10, 1);
        r = Math.round(50 * (1 - Math.min(intensity, 1)));
        g = Math.round(255 * Math.min(intensity * 2, 1));
        b = Math.round(50 * (1 - Math.min(intensity, 1)));
    }

    const backgroundColor = `rgb(${r}, ${g}, ${b})`;
    const brightness = (r * 299 + g * 587 + b * 114) / 1000;
    const color = brightness > 155 ? '#000000' : '#ffffff';

    return { backgroundColor, color };
}
```

